1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,686
NYPD's protest unit.

2
00:00:02,831 --> 00:00:03,495
Disbanded.

3
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:05,842
Mamdani keeps a campaign promise.

4
00:00:07,867 --> 00:00:11,056
On Monday, November 16, New
York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani

5
00:00:11,056 --> 00:00:13,641
and Police Commissioner
Jessica Tisch announced

6
00:00:13,641 --> 00:00:16,885
that the NYPD's Strategic
Response Group will be disbanded.

7
00:00:17,105 --> 00:00:18,816
The changes begin in January.

8
00:00:19,066 --> 00:00:22,899
The Strategic Response Group is the unit
that responds to citywide protests,

9
00:00:22,899 --> 00:00:25,925
civil disorder and major events,
with specialized equipment.

10
00:00:26,145 --> 00:00:29,112
Disbanding it was one
of Mamdani's campaign promises.

11
00:00:29,332 --> 00:00:32,436
Back in January, he said he still
believed the city needed to disband it.

12
00:00:32,656 --> 00:00:34,814
Now he says protests should not be met

13
00:00:34,814 --> 00:00:37,767
with the same police response
as a terrorism threat.

14
00:00:38,867 --> 00:00:42,406
So what replaces it? First,
a civilian-led Community Dialogue

15
00:00:42,406 --> 00:00:46,699
and De-escalation Division, inside
the mayor's Office of Community Safety.

16
00:00:46,919 --> 00:00:49,659
Its members carry no weapons
and have no arrest powers.

17
00:00:49,909 --> 00:00:51,671
Inside the police department,

18
00:00:51,671 --> 00:00:55,317
a new First Amendment Support
Team of 30 uniformed officers,

19
00:00:55,317 --> 00:00:59,328
trained in communication
and de-escalation, will work at protests.

20
00:00:59,548 --> 00:01:02,572
Counterterrorism work, including
heavy-weapons deployments,

21
00:01:02,572 --> 00:01:06,006
moves to the department's Intelligence
and Counterterrorism Bureau.

22
00:01:06,226 --> 00:01:08,640
A new Patrol Support
Division will give mostly

23
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:11,263
patrol officers special
crowd-management training.

24
00:01:11,483 --> 00:01:14,936
There are also new limits on tools
like pepper spray during protests.

25
00:01:15,156 --> 00:01:18,220
The city says all of this
comes at no additional cost,

26
00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:20,206
with no officers hired or laid off.

27
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:23,823
Why was this unit so controversial?

28
00:01:24,043 --> 00:01:28,257
During the 2020 George Floyd
protests, the Strategic Response Group

29
00:01:28,257 --> 00:01:32,281
was accused of unlawfully detaining
more than 100 demonstrators.

30
00:01:32,531 --> 00:01:35,564
A legal settlement announced
in 2023 was described

31
00:01:35,564 --> 00:01:38,232
in part as reparations
for those detentions.

32
00:01:38,452 --> 00:01:41,262
It now governs how and when
the police can deploy the unit.

33
00:01:41,482 --> 00:01:45,290
That same year, the unit skipped
a City Council public safety hearing,

34
00:01:45,290 --> 00:01:48,663
citing ongoing litigation,
and sent written testimony instead.

35
00:01:49,767 --> 00:01:51,497
Commissioner Tisch backs the plan.

36
00:01:51,717 --> 00:01:54,168
She said she would never support
changes that diminish

37
00:01:54,168 --> 00:01:57,392
the department's ability to protect
New Yorkers, and that these changes

38
00:01:57,392 --> 00:01:59,707
will make it a stronger,
more effective department.

39
00:01:59,957 --> 00:02:01,557
The police union disagrees.

40
00:02:01,777 --> 00:02:05,613
Its president, Patrick Hendry, said
today is not a good day for New Yorkers,

41
00:02:05,613 --> 00:02:08,187
and accused the mayor
of putting public and officer

42
00:02:08,187 --> 00:02:10,357
safety at risk to appease
his radical base.

43
00:02:10,577 --> 00:02:13,235
City Council Member Phil Wong
wants to keep the unit,

44
00:02:13,235 --> 00:02:16,997
create a separate team for street
takeovers, and hire more police officers.

45
00:02:17,217 --> 00:02:19,529
On the mayor's side,
the argument is that protest

46
00:02:19,529 --> 00:02:22,077
policing and counterterrorism
should be separate jobs.

47
00:02:22,297 --> 00:02:24,685
No statement has been found yet
from civil liberties groups

48
00:02:24,685 --> 00:02:25,657
or from the White House.

49
00:02:26,767 --> 00:02:30,109
What comes next? The reforms
begin in January.

50
00:02:30,329 --> 00:02:33,571
No City Council vote,
budget line or legislative

51
00:02:33,571 --> 00:02:35,935
timeline has been described so far.

52
00:02:36,185 --> 00:02:41,124
It is also not clear yet whether
the 2023 settlement will need to change.

53
00:02:41,344 --> 00:02:44,758
One thing seems certain:
the fight between the mayor,

54
00:02:44,758 --> 00:02:48,558
the police union and some
council members is far from over.

55
00:02:49,967 --> 00:02:52,132
Was ending the SRG the right call?

56
00:02:52,352 --> 00:02:53,381
Tell me in the comments.
